Anyone out there knows of a mechanical woman who is looking for a boyfriend.

525
00:40:42,320 --> 00:40:47,480
The robot is a powerful symbol of the world of tomorrow.

526
00:40:47,900 --> 00:40:49,960
We're still waiting around, most of us.

527
00:40:49,961 --> 00:40:58,376
I don't know if you've got one, but I think we're still waiting around for our own personal robots to hang around our house and service our coffee in the morning and

528
00:40:58,377 --> 00:40:59,600
take the dog for a walk.

529
00:40:59,601 --> 00:41:04,380
All of those things were supposed to have been here by now, and they're not.

530
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:09,940
Inventors predicted time-saving gadgets would create unprecedented leisure time.

531
00:41:10,700 --> 00:41:14,820
In fact, downtime has decreased, despite the advance of technology.

532
00:41:15,580 --> 00:41:20,200
...will be washed, even egg stains removed by washers that require no cleansing agent.

533
00:41:20,740 --> 00:41:24,040
High-frequency sound waves dissolve food particles and dirt.

534
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:28,940
Inventors always claim that their devices are going to save you something.

535
00:41:28,941 --> 00:41:32,980
It's going to save you labor, it's going to save you time, it's going to save you drudgery.

536
00:41:33,380 --> 00:41:38,960
But because you can do it more often, you do do it more often, and so you don't end up saving time.

537
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:47,160
And so even successful inventions can be regarded as failures because they really haven't saved you anything.

538
00:41:48,420 --> 00:41:55,900
Major corporations oftentimes used the house of the future as a draw, as they became containers of magical devices.

539
00:41:58,940 --> 00:42:01,940
Would I like it?

