00:42:33,741 --> 00:42:37,300
nobody really wants to live in something that looks like that people just wanted

549
00:42:37,301 --> 00:42:41,300
something that looked like everybody else's I think even when their

550
00:42:41,301 --> 00:42:45,080
inventions don't really happen they've always provided us with something to

551
00:42:45,081 --> 00:42:50,900
think about I think when we look at a lot of failed inventions or innovations

552
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:56,220
that went nowhere we are tempted to see it as a history of failure but that's

553
00:42:56,221 --> 00:42:58,260
It's not really what it is at all.

554
00:42:58,261 --> 00:43:01,320
In fact, these are kind of testimonies to the human

555
00:43:01,321 --> 00:43:07,240
spirit without the courage to fail, without the courage to try something that may or may

556
00:43:07,241 --> 00:43:12,240
not work. We'd never enjoy the progress that we have.

557
00:43:12,241 --> 00:43:19,145
We should look at people who are great minds, great thinkers, look at what they did.

